dcast where we dig deeper into the latest cyber threats and security chall=
enges=2C and provide analysis that can help in securing the online world.=
 This week we look at a well-known but still unsolved problem on the Inter=
net=2C namely=2C overly descriptive host naming practices. These create hi=
gher cybersecurity risks for organizations that are probably revealing too=
 much about their own DNS infrastructure. Listen to WhoisXML API CEO & Fou=
nder Jonathan Zhang and Advanced Threat Researcher Ed Gibbs talk about how=
 companies are exposing their internet infrastructure with overly exposed=
 descriptive DNS naming practices and the associated cybersecurity & other=
 risks. (https://soundcloud.com/whoisxml/overly-exposed-dns-infrastructure=
-too-much-info-for-the-bad-guys?mc=3Dmail_campaign&mc_cid=3D54d78454c1&mc_=
eid=3DUNIQID)
